{
  "an8.73:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 8.73 ",
  "an8.73:0.2": "8. Pairs ",
  "an8.73:0.3": "Mindfulness of Death (1st) ",
  "an8.73:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying at Ñātika in the brick house. ",
  "an8.73:1.2": "There the Buddha addressed the mendicants, ",
  "an8.73:1.3": "“Mendicants!” ",
  "an8.73:1.4": "“Venerable sir,” they replied. ",
  "an8.73:1.5": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "an8.73:1.6": "“Mendicants, when mindfulness of death is developed and cultivated it’s very fruitful and beneficial. It has freedom from death as its objective and culmination. ",
  "an8.73:1.7": "But do you develop mindfulness of death?” ",
  "an8.73:2.1": "When he said this, one of the mendicants said to the Buddha, ",
  "an8.73:2.2": "“Sir, I develop mindfulness of death.” ",
  "an8.73:2.3": "“But mendicant, how do you develop it?” ",
  "an8.73:2.4": "“In this case, sir, I think: ",
  "an8.73:2.5": "‘Oh, if I’d only live for another day and night, I’d focus on the Buddha’s instructions and I could really achieve a lot.’ ",
  "an8.73:2.6": "That’s how I develop mindfulness of death.” ",
  "an8.73:3.1": "Another mendicant said to the Buddha, ",
  "an8.73:3.2": "“Sir, I too develop mindfulness of death.” ",
  "an8.73:3.3": "“But mendicant, how do you develop it?” ",
  "an8.73:3.4": "“In this case, sir, I think: ",
  "an8.73:3.5": "‘Oh, if I’d only live for another day, I’d focus on the Buddha’s instructions and I could really achieve a lot.’ ",
  "an8.73:3.6":